# What the builder is sent.
#
# Deliberately a list of what to LEAVE OUT rather than what to include,
# because the Dockerfile already says what it copies and a second include list
# would be a second place to forget something.
#
# This matters more than it looks. The context is uploaded to Fly's remote
# builder on every deploy, and it was 380 MB across 4,525 files: 225 MB of
# archived Unity assets, 149 MB of git history and 5 MB of mockups, none of
# which any stage of the build touches. A deploy that waits five minutes for a
# builder and then uploads 380 MB has a lot of surface for a transient failure
# to land on, and run 79 is what that looks like.

# Build output and dependencies: every stage installs its own.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/target

# The archived Unity game. It is the REFERENCE the rebuild is read from, never
# anything the image runs.
archive-model

# History, notes and explorations. The image needs the sources, not the story.
.git
.github
mockups
docs
prototype
*.md

# Tests run in CI, not in the image.
**/tests
web/tests

# Local databases and editor noise.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
.DS_Store
*.log
